    "result_text": "All 55 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the six structured-address checkpoints (Cp01, Cp12, Cp29, Cp30, Cp36, Cp44) and no regressions in the rest.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to `POST /api/owners` (and the `PUT` path), keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n**Schema / DTO** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added `addressLine1` (optional) and `addressLine2` (optional) to `OwnerFields`; documented `address` as an accepted flat input that on response is the composed normalized value.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list, since an owner may now supply its address structurally. `city` stays required. The DTO is regenerated by the build.\n\n**Address logic** (`OwnerAddress.normalize`)\n- Normalizes whichever fields are supplied (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET` etc.), clearing blank lines to `null`.\n- Prefers the structured fields: when `addressLine1` is non-blank, the composed `address` = normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space + normalized `addressLine2` appended when present; otherwise it falls back to the normalized flat `address`.\n- Because the composed `address` is non-blank exactly when an address was supplied in either form, `ValidateOwnerFields`' existing single `address` required-check now enforces \"address in either form, plus city\" unchanged.\n\n**Persistence & mapping**\n- Added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` fields, getters/setters, and `@Column`s to `Owner`; MapStruct maps them by name into and out of the DTO, so they round-trip and are returned by `GET`.\n- Added `address_line1`/`address_line2` columns (at the end of the `owners` table) to all four DB schemas, and updated the positional hsqldb seed inserts (the only ones matching the full schema) to match.\n- `ValidateOwner` now also normalizes/composes the address, and `ApplyOwner` copies the line fields, so the `PUT` pipeline stays consistent.\n\nEverything that reads the address for household hash, postcode validation and locality continues to key off `city`/`postcode`, which are present in both forms.",
